# `yo fix <path> --migrate mutable-globals` (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md
# decision 47): a module-level or `thread_local` runtime binding is immutable
# unless declared `mut(name)`, so every global written after its initializer
# (reassigned, a field write, a `&mut` lend, a `&mut self` call) gets the
# marker (E0917 otherwise), in each declaration form. A `ref` handle mutated
# through its methods (`names`) and a global only read (`fixed`) stay
# unmarked; reassigning a handle (`replaced`) needs it. The expected_tree pins
# the rewritten main.yo; the trailing `check` proves no write is left.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=180
